The current implementations follow the bitwire 0.5.0 contract. Independent message bytes and conformance cases are from bitwire's layered contract at 1974ce38c4016b4ba57c415bcbc7e1a5111713dd, also Apache-2.0.

The TypeScript WebSocket host-effect and lifecycle implementation and its local TLS test fixtures derive from the system2 experiment at a866f502933a43d4e24eda7bc01e4aabf38073b8 (Bitspark, 2026), adapted to the shared contract. The fixture private key is public test data only.

Earlier runtime implementations included code from nightseam v0.6.0, commit 5cc9723a24646c40ed1861f892b2b23eb6d785d7, Copyright 2026 Bitspark and the nightseam contributors, Apache-2.0. Those implementations have been replaced; their source and attribution remain recorded in Git history.
